WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.709 --> 00:00:14.457
The was as fast as the Mongolia, but not as comfortable for Aouda as Mr.

2
00:00:14.497 --> 00:00:15.318
Fogg would have liked.

3
00:00:17.339 --> 00:00:22.483
However, the trip from Calcutta to Hong Kong would take only ten or twelve days, and Aouda was

4
00:00:22.583 --> 00:00:23.644
not difficult to please.

5
00:00:25.185 --> 00:00:29.528
During the first few days of the journey, Aouda became better acquainted with her protector, Mr.

6
00:00:29.548 --> 00:00:36.017
Fogg. She frequently expressed her deep gratitude for his efforts in saving her from a horrible fate.

7
00:00:37.518 --> 00:00:42.279
Mr. Fogg listened to her without the slightest apparent emotion, but he seemed to be always on the

8
00:00:42.319 --> 00:00:43.840
watch for her care and comfort.

9
00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:50.162
He visited her regularly each day, not so much to talk himself, but to sit and listen to

10
00:00:50.202 --> 00:00:53.963
her. He treated her with the strictest politeness.

11
00:00:55.823 --> 00:00:57.804
Aouda did not quite know what to make of him.

12
00:00:59.232 --> 00:01:02.614
Passepartout had given her some hints of his master's eccentricity.

13
00:01:04.315 --> 00:01:08.298
She had smiled when she heard of the wager that was sending the two men around the world.

14
00:01:09.799 --> 00:01:13.221
Detective Fix had managed to board the boat at the last possible moment.

15
00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:16.523
He had left orders that the warrant for Mr.

16
00:01:16.563 --> 00:01:19.445
Fogg's arrest should be forwarded to him in Hong Kong.

17
00:01:21.025 --> 00:01:24.768
He was hoping to conceal his presence on the Rangoon until the end of the voyage.

18
00:01:26.608 --> 00:01:29.471
All Fix's hopes and wishes were now centered on Hong Kong.

19
00:01:31.052 --> 00:01:34.876
The steamer would be stopping in Singapore, but the stay there would be too brief for him to

20
00:01:34.936 --> 00:01:35.536
arrest Mr.

21
00:01:35.556 --> 00:01:42.723
Fogg. "Now, either the warrant will be at Hong Kong, in which case I shall finally be able

22
00:01:42.783 --> 00:01:46.727
to arrest my man, or it will not be there," thought Fix.

23
00:01:47.748 --> 00:01:52.032
"If it's not there, it is absolutely necessary that I delay his departure.

24
00:01:53.328 --> 00:01:56.530
I have failed at Bombay, and I have failed at Calcutta.

25
00:01:57.610 --> 00:02:00.632
If I fail at Hong Kong, my reputation is lost!

26
00:02:01.793 --> 00:02:04.534
Cost what it may, I must succeed!"

27
00:02:06.355 --> 00:02:11.598
As he puzzled over his predicament, Fix decided that he must make a confidant of Passepartout.

28
00:02:13.179 --> 00:02:15.440
He was certain that Passepartout was not Mr.

29
00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:16.981
Fogg's accomplice in crime.

30
00:02:17.001 --> 00:02:22.304
"I will tell him what kind of man his master is," Fix thought.

31
00:02:23.948 --> 00:02:26.389
"When Passepartout finds out how Mr.

32
00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:32.793
Fogg really makes his money, the servant will fear being accused himself and become my ally."

33
00:02:34.214 --> 00:02:36.815
But this strategy was risky, Fix realized.

34
00:02:36.835 --> 00:02:42.518
"One word of warning from Passepartout to his master and all will be ruined!"

35
00:02:43.279 --> 00:02:46.901
There was no denying it—the detective was in a difficult position.

36
00:02:48.662 --> 00:02:52.164
One day Fix emerged from his cabin and went on deck to get some air.

37
00:02:54.228 --> 00:02:58.931
Passepartout was walking up and down in the forward part of the steamer when Fix rushed up to

38
00:02:58.971 --> 00:03:00.192
him, faking surprise.

39
00:03:00.212 --> 00:03:03.755
"You? Here, on the Rangoon?"

40
00:03:04.155 --> 00:03:04.615
he said.

41
00:03:04.635 --> 00:03:07.838
"What, Monsieur Fix, are you onboard?"

42
00:03:08.218 --> 00:03:09.799
said the astonished Passepartout.

43
00:03:09.819 --> 00:03:13.942
"Why, I left you at Bombay, and here you are, on the way to Hong Kong!

44
00:03:14.682 --> 00:03:15.943
Are you going around the world too?"

45
00:03:15.963 --> 00:03:18.745
"No, no," replied Fix.

46
00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:22.488
"I shall stop at Hong Kong, at least for some days."

47
00:03:23.808 --> 00:03:25.489
"Hmm," said Passepartout.

48
00:03:25.509 --> 00:03:29.031
"But why haven't I seen you onboard since we left Calcutta?"

49
00:03:31.012 --> 00:03:32.693
"Oh, a bit of sea sickness.

50
00:03:33.673 --> 00:03:36.135
I've been staying in my cabin," replied Fix.

51
00:03:36.155 --> 00:03:38.376
"And how is Mr.

52
00:03:38.436 --> 00:03:42.978
Fogg?" "As well and as punctual as ever," replied Passepartout.

53
00:03:43.159 --> 00:03:44.399
"Not a day behind time!"

54
00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:52.584
Passepartout went on to explain Aouda's presence among them, and Fix, as usual, invited Passepartout for a drink

55
00:03:52.624 --> 00:03:52.964
in the bar.

56
00:03:55.040 --> 00:04:00.324
Later that night as he lay in bed, Passepartout puzzled over the strange coincidence that had kept Fix

57
00:04:00.384 --> 00:04:01.965
on the same route as his master.

58
00:04:03.766 --> 00:04:09.169
Passepartout wondered why this very friendly person, whom he had met at Suez and then encountered onboard the

59
00:04:09.209 --> 00:04:16.114
Mongolia, now turned up unexpectedly on the Rangoon despite having told Passepartout that Bombay was his destination.

60
00:04:17.354 --> 00:04:18.435
Was he following Mr.

61
00:04:18.475 --> 00:04:19.456
Fogg step by step?

62
00:04:21.132 --> 00:04:25.695
Passepartout was ready to wager that Fix would also leave Hong Kong at the same time as Mr.

63
00:04:25.735 --> 00:04:28.156
Fogg and probably on the same steamer!

64
00:04:29.757 --> 00:04:33.178
Passepartout realized Fix must be an agent from the Reform Club.

65
00:04:34.619 --> 00:04:36.760
He must be a spy sent to make sure that Mr.

66
00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:39.222
Fogg really went around the world, as was agreed.

67
00:04:39.242 --> 00:04:41.583
"It's clear!"

68
00:04:41.863 --> 00:04:44.484
thought Passepartout, satisfied with his own shrewdness.

69
00:04:45.825 --> 00:04:47.546
"He has been sent to keep us in view!

70
00:04:48.787 --> 00:04:50.768
Mr. Fogg is such an honorable man!

71
00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:53.625
This is not the proper thing for them to do at all!

72
00:04:54.986 --> 00:05:00.269
Well, gentlemen of the Reform Club," decided Passepartout, "this shall cost you dearly."

73
00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:04.271
He was determined to tease Fix when he got the chance.

74
00:05:06.633 --> 00:05:12.076
On the afternoon of Wednesday, October 30, the Rangoon, now half a day ahead of schedule, arrived in

75
00:05:12.136 --> 00:05:21.888
Singapore. Phileas Fogg noted this arrival in his journal and then walked ashore, accompanied by Aouda.

76
00:05:21.908 --> 00:05:26.971
I spent the last five days on a steamer called the Rangoon, traveling from Calcutta to Hong Kong.

77
00:05:28.191 --> 00:05:31.653
This steamer wasn't as luxurious as it could have been, but it wasn't too bad.

78
00:05:33.234 --> 00:05:37.496
Steamers, also known as steamboats or steamships, are the most common type of boat in the world.

79
00:05:38.777 --> 00:05:44.339
They are used not only to carry passengers, but also to transport goods such as coffee, tea, silk,

80
00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:45.120
and spices.

81
00:05:46.556 --> 00:05:50.998
In fact, steamers have allowed global trade to increase quite rapidly since they were first used in the

82
00:05:51.058 --> 00:05:51.939
early 1800s.

83
00:05:53.239 --> 00:05:57.922
Today steamers come in all shapes and sizes, and sail on canals, rivers, and oceans.

84
00:05:59.383 --> 00:06:02.024
They can travel large distances cheaply and safely.
